From ed5ebfafadb310930b316a343bdef835f55bbc57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add a sensor register blob parser

Some sensors have no public register documentation, so their register
sequences cannot be part of the kernel source. Add a small header-only
parser for a versioned binary file that carries those sequences, so a
sensor driver can load them with request_firmware().

The blob holds an identification register and value, init, stream on and
stream off operation lists, a table of exposure, gain and frame length
control registers, and a table of modes with their geometry, link
frequency, pixel rate and per-mode operation list. The layout is
documented at the top of the header. The parser verifies the magic,
version, size and CRC, bounds-checks every offset and count and rejects
unknown operation codes, so the accessors never read outside the file.

No user is added by this patch.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 MAINTAINERS                        |   1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/sensor-regblob.h | 362 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 363 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/sensor-regblob.h

